  "question": {
    "text": "Number of integral terms in the expansion of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><msup><mn>7</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>11</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mfenced></msup></mrow></mfenced><mn>824</mn></msup></math> is equal to ______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "138",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We know that,</p><p>General term in expansion of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>7</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>11</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mn>824</mn></msup></math> is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mi>r</mi><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>824</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>·</mo><msup><mn>7</mn><mfrac><mrow><mn>824</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>·</mo><msup><mn>11</mn><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p><p>For integral term, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> must be multiple of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> and should be less than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>824</mn></math></p><p>So, the series will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo> </mo><mn>822</mn></math></p><p>Now, finding number of terms we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>822</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>137</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>138</mn></math></p><p>Hence, total integral terms will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>138</mn></math></p>"
  }
}